 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Staff Record Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an employee information form?\", \"a\": \"An employee information form is the record an employer keeps on each person: legal name, contact details, job title, start date, and emergency contacts. HR collects it at hiring and goes back to it whenever payroll or a manager needs a detail.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an employee information form online?\", \"a\": \"List the fields payroll and HR use, decide who may see each one, then put a database behind the form. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> creates the form, the employee record, and the yearly confirmation from one description.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do I need on an employee information form to put someone on payroll?\", \"a\": \"Payroll needs the person's legal name and Social Security number as shown on their card, a home address, and a signed Form W-4. Employers also complete Form I-9, and many collect bank details through a direct deposit form. An app built on Emergent can pass those fields straight to your payroll system through its API.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to fill out an employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Write your legal name exactly as it reads on your Social Security card, then a current home address and a phone you answer. Most versions also ask for an emergency contact and end with your signature and the date. If a field is unclear, ask HR before guessing, since payroll copies these answers as written.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there an employee information form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A typical employee information form template fits on one page, grouped by section, with a signature line at the bottom. Paper suits a small team. Past a few dozen people, keeping every copy current becomes the hard part.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I customize an employee information form template for my company?\", \"a\": \"Cut every field nobody reads, then add the ones HR and payroll use, such as department and work location. Move private details like date of birth into their own section so fewer people handle them. A static employee information form PDF makes each of these changes slow, because every edit means a new file and every answer still gets retyped into payroll.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Several template sites let you download a free employee information form. Emergent is free to start as well, and its free tier covers building and publishing an online version that saves each answer to a record you can update.\"}, {\"q\": \"Who should have access to an employee information form?\", \"a\": \"Only the people whose work depends on a given field. HR and payroll need the full record, while a manager rarely needs more than work contact details. Keep Social Security numbers and bank details behind the tightest access, and store any paper copies in a locked file. Records kept in an Emergent app sit in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"What goes on a basic new employee information form?\", \"a\": \"A basic version asks for legal name, address, phone, personal email, date of birth, job title, start date, and one emergency contact. Tax and work eligibility forms travel with it in a new employee form packet.\"}, {\"q\": \"How often should an employee information form be updated?\", \"a\": \"Once a year at minimum, when each employee checks their own record, and again whenever an address or phone number changes. Supervisors who need emergency contacts on site can keep a separate emergency contact form at the front desk.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
